    "v2_status": "dropped-still-material",
    "residuals": [
     "must_not_contain item 'No dry skin elsewhere on the body, asserted as a clean negative' (and the matching salience_trap) is not a genuine error: the patient's reply actually opens with a clear negative - 'Uh, no not really' - before the garbled fragment. The fact sheet quotes only 'I have <INAUDIBLE_SPEECH/> <UNSURE>skin really dry</UNSURE> now' and omits that leading denial, so a scribe recording 'no dry skin elsewhere' would be wrongly penalised."
    ],
    "excise_classifier_verdicts": [
     "touches_mc_or_traps"
    ],
    "why_not_excisable": "at least one residual touches must_contain or salience_traps"
   },
   "day4_consultation01": {
    "status": "dropped-still-material",
    "v1_status": "revised-kept",
    "v2_status": "revised-kept",
    "residuals": [
     "must_contain item \"The patient reports no other unusual symptoms besides those described\" conflicts with the must_contain nausea item: in the same turn the patient says \"nothing, else unusual\" and then immediately volunteers nausea. As stated it is a required fact that the transcript partially contradicts, and a scribe recording \"no other symptoms\" would be both rewarded and (via the nausea fact) penalised."
    ],
    "excise_classifier_verdicts": [
     "touches_mc_or_traps"
    ],
    "why_not_excisable": "at least one residual touches must_contain or salience_traps"
